  "notes": "Clinical_content normative source; normative strength PROHIBITION; permitted_use prohibited_autonomous_rule. Architecture references are intentionally empty: per v1.2 §4.3 clinical-content rules cite valid evidence_claim_ids and do not carry architecture refs (none in §13.6); [] means 'none in source', not 'missing'. Evidence grade/role preserved per source: QRF-028 (X1; indirect/extrapolated) — general sprint-ratio evidence only, not RF-specific dosing or progression authority. Source ratios preserved exactly from §13.6: 1:3, 1:5, and 1:7. Per §13.6 behavior preserved exactly: 1:3, 1:5, and 1:7 sprint work-to-rest ratios must not become RF-specific autonomous dosing rules. The ratios must not become automatic sprint prescription, universal RF work-to-rest rules, universal sprint-progression rules, phase-entry/exit criteria, readiness evidence by themselves, or return-to-running/sprinting/training/sport rules; they clear no field domain not directly tested. The rule creates no sprint/running dosing, work-to-rest dosing, progression, exercise selection, field plan, complete rehab plan, RTT, or RTS, and sprint-ratio completion alone is neither progression authority nor readiness; it aligns with v1.2 §17 case 27 (blocked 1:3/1:5/1:7 RF sprint dosing appears -> CI fails) and Appendix C. Safety-state choice (read §13.6 exactly): §13.6 does NOT assign a closed V3.1 safety state, so safety_state_output is null and blocked_targets is empty, and the sprint work-to-rest ratio prohibition is represented in decision_contract; no safety state was inferred by analogy. It does not override RF-FIELD-001/002/003/004, RF-RECUR-002, or RF-REHAB-004, and does not bypass RF-FIELD-001/002/003/004, RF-RECUR-001/002, RF-REHAB-001..006, RF-SEV-005, RF-DX-006, or RF-SAF-006; uncertainty is preserved when sprint-ratio source quality, sprint exposure, speed, rest-structure, symptom/next-day response, capacity, field-domain, schedule, monitoring, or sport-demand evidence is incomplete. Sprint-dosage prohibition rule, not a safety rule. No sprint-dosage or field-exposure engine is authored here (deferred to the later field, rehab, and readiness objects). Draft — approval_status remains pending."
